        // after possible rotation, handle lagPump recompute based on events
        // events: leadPump changed (i.e., leadPump <> prevLeadPump) OR effectiveDemand > prevRunningCount
        // Note: we already might have recomputed lagPump in rotation case if leadPump changed.
        // However, we also need to recompute if effectiveDemand increased (i.e., demand up).
        // In both cases we recompute lagPump accordingly; else keep previous lagPump.
        // But we must be careful: If rotation didn't happen, but effectiveDemand increased, we need to recompute lagPump as min among others (excluding leadPump). So implement accordingly.

        if effectiveDemand >= 2 then
